\title{Exterior covectors and transported singlets}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{An invariant alternating form supplies a matter
polynomial of exterior degree two. Its construction must
still make sense when two is not invertible. The same
coefficient ring also determines what an alternating
contraction of two separately transported fields means.}

